## LuminOS live medium only.
##
## The installer has to partition disks, mount targets and run pacstrap, all of
## which need root. The live user must therefore be able to escalate without a
## password, because there IS no password to type: this is an anonymous live
## session that anyone who boots the medium is already sitting in front of.
##
## This file is scoped to the live image and is NOT copied to the installed
## system. The installer creates the real user with a real password and normal
## password-prompting sudo. If you ever find this file on an installed LuminOS,
## that is a bug in the installer, not a policy here.
%wheel ALL=(ALL:ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
